The failing **Fabbot / Checks** run is a `codespell` false positive, unrelated to this change: it flags the pre-existing `Schema::hasTable()` calls in `Connection.php` (line 350) and `ConnectionTest.php` (lines 701, 727) as a typo for `hashtable`, which is not a real method and would break the code if applied.

This is a known issue that's already fixed on newer branches via `.codespellrc` (`ignore-words-list = smove,hastable`), present on `7.4`, `8.1` and `8.2` — but that file was never backported to `6.4`, so any PR touching a file with `hasTable()` on this branch hits it. All substantive checks (Unit Tests on PHP 8.1–8.6, PHPStan, Psalm, Hardening tests, Verify Packages) pass; only this lint false positive is red.

Happy to add `.codespellrc` to `6.4` in this PR (or a separate tiny PR) if that's preferred — let me know.

